---
title: ONI interleave
tags: tools
heading: "Interleave"
summary: >-
    Interleaves the characters of two strings, with an optional delimiter.
---
{% from "macros/tool.njk" import toolSection with context %}
{% from "macros/tool-frame.njk" import toolFrame %}
{% set filename = page.fileSlug %}
{% set intro %}
    <p>Takes a character from First, then one from Second, and so on, so <code class="tool-example">HLOWRD</code> and <code class="tool-example">EL OL</code> give <code class="tool-example">HELLO WORLD</code>. When one string is longer, the rest of it is added on the end. Swap changes which string goes first.</p>
    <p>A delimiter goes between every character, such as a space, which can make interleaved hex easier to read.</p>
    <p>In the browser console: <code class="tool-example">convrtr.{{ filename }}(string1, string2, delimiter = "")</code></p>
{% endset %}
{% call toolSection(intro) %}
{% call toolFrame(filename, "Interleave", inputs = [{ label: "First", placeholder: "Example: HLOWRD" }, { label: "Second", placeholder: "Example: EL OL" }], swap = true, actions = [{ id: filename + "Run", label: "Interleave" }]) %}
<div class="tool-field tool-field--short">
    <div class="tool-field__head">
        <label class="tool-field__label" for="{{ filename }}Delimiter">Delimiter</label>
    </div>
    <input type="text" class="form-control" id="{{ filename }}Delimiter" autocomplete="off" aria-describedby="{{ filename }}DelimiterNote">
    <span class="tool-field__note" id="{{ filename }}DelimiterNote">Between every character. Leave empty for none.</span>
</div>
{% endcall %}
{% endcall %}
